<exercise>
<statement>
			<p>
				Solve the initial value problem <md>{\vec{x}}' = \begin{bmatrix} -3 &amp; -12 \\ 3 &amp; 9 \end{bmatrix}\vec{x} \qquad \vec{x}(0) = \begin{bmatrix} 3 \\ 2  \end{bmatrix}</md> and sketch the phase portrait for this system.
			</p>
</statement>

<answer>			<p>
				 <m>\vec{x}(t) = \left[\begin{smallmatrix} (-42t+3)e^{3t} \\ (21t + 2)e^{3t} \end{smallmatrix}\right]</m> 
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-n3-12-3-9">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>{\vec{x}}' = \begin{bmatrix} -3 &amp; -12 \\ 3 &amp; 9 \end{bmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
