	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			What is/are the defect(s) of the eigenvalue(s)?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			Eigenvalue 2 has a defect of 2
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of <m>{\vec{x}}' = A \vec{x}</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>\vec{x} =
C_1
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 \\ 3 \\ 1
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
e^{2t}
+
C_2
\left(
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 \\ -1 \\ 0
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
+
t
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 \\ 3 \\ 1
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
\right)
e^{2t}
+
C_3
\left(
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
1 \\ 0 \\ 0
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
+
t
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 \\ -1 \\ 0
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
+
\frac{t^2}{2}
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 \\ 3 \\ 1
\end{smallmatrix}\right]
\right)
e^{2t}</m>
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
</exercise>



<exercise>
<introduction>
	<p>
				Let <m>A = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
0 &amp; 4 &amp; -2 \\
-1 &amp; -4 &amp; 1 \\
0 &amp; 0 &amp; -2
\end{smallmatrix} \right]</m>.
			</p>
</introduction>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			What are the eigenvalues?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			-2 
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			What is/are the defect(s) of the eigenvalue(s)?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			Defect 1
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of <m>{\vec{x}}' = A \vec{x}</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>\vec{x}(t) = C_1 \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{-2t} + C_2\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 \\1 \\ 2 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{-2t} + C_3\left( \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 2 \\ -1 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]te^{-2t} + \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{-2t}\right)</m> 
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
	<p>
				Let <m>A = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
2 &amp; 1 &amp; -1 \\
-1 &amp; 0 &amp; 2 \\
-1 &amp; -2 &amp; 4
\end{smallmatrix} \right]</m>.
			</p>
</introduction>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			What are the eigenvalues?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			2
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			What is/are the defect(s) of the eigenvalue(s)?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			Defect of 2
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of <m>{\vec{x}}' = A \vec{x}</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>\vec{x}(t) = C_1 \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{2t} + C_2\left(\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 \\1 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]te^{2t} + \left[\begin{smallmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{2t}\right) + C_3\left(\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 \\1 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]\frac{t^2}{2}e^{2t} + \left[\begin{smallmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]te^{2t} + \left[\begin{smallmatrix} -1 \\-1 \\0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{2t}\right)</m> 
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<statement>
			<p>
				Suppose that <m>A</m> is a <m>2 \times 2</m> matrix with a repeated eigenvalue <m>\lambda</m>. Suppose that there are two linearly independent eigenvectors. Show that <m>A = \lambda I</m>.
			</p>
</statement>

<answer>			<p>
				 Hint: This means everything is an eigenvector. Or, this can be set up as a system of equations. 
			</p>
</answer>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
			<p>
				Let <m>A =
\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
a &amp; a \\
b &amp; c
\end{smallmatrix}\right]</m>, where <m>a</m>, <m>b</m>, and <m>c</m> are unknowns. Suppose that <m>5</m> is a doubled eigenvalue of defect 1, and suppose that <m>\left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
1 \\ 0
\end{smallmatrix}\right]</m> is a corresponding eigenvector. Find <m>A</m> and show that there is only one such matrix <m>A</m>.
			</p>
</statement>
<answer>
	<p>
		<m>A = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix}
5 &amp; 5 \\ 0 &amp; 5
\end{smallmatrix}\right]</m>
	</p>
</answer>

</exercise>
<exercise>
<introduction>
			<p>
				For each system, 
				<ul>
					<li>
						<p>
							classify the system according to type as one of sink/source/saddle/center/ spiral source/spiral sink,
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p>
							solve the system, and 
						</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<p>
							sketch the phase portrait.
						</p>
					</li>
				</ul>
				Both real and complex eigenvalues appear.
			</p>
		</introduction>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; 0 \\ 1 &amp; 1 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				Nodal Source,\ <m>C_1\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{2t} + C_2\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^t</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-2-0-1-1">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 2 &amp; 0 \\ 1 &amp; 1 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_2_0_1_1_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} -2&amp; -2\\ 8&amp; -2\end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				 Spiral Sink, <m>C_1e^{-2t}\left[\begin{smallmatrix} -\sin(4t) \\ 2\cos(4t) \end{smallmatrix}\right] + C_2e^{-2t}\left[\begin{smallmatrix} \cos(4t) \\ 2\sin(4t) \end{smallmatrix}\right]</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-n2-n2-8-n2">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} -2&amp; -2\\ 8&amp; -2\end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_n2_n2_8_n2_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 5\\ -5&amp; -3  \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				Center, <m>C_1\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 5\cos(4t) \\ -3\cos(4t) = 4\sin(4t) \end{smallmatrix}\right] + C_2 \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 5\sin(4t)\\ 4\cos(4t) - 3\sin(4t) \end{smallmatrix}\right]</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-3-5-n5-n3">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 5\\ -5&amp; -3  \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_3_5_n5_n3_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}' = \begin{pmatrix} -1 &amp; -3 \\ 3 &amp; -7 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				 Improper Nodal Source, <m>C_1\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{4t} + C_2\left(\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 1  \end{smallmatrix}\right]te^{4t} + \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1/3 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{4t}\right)</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-n1-n1-3-n7">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}' = \begin{pmatrix} -1 &amp; -3 \\ 3 &amp; -7 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>.</caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_n1_n3_3_n7_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 2\\ 0&amp;-2 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m> 
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				Saddle, <m>C_1\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{3t} + C_2\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 2 \\ -5 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{-2t}</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-3-0-2-n2">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 2\\ 0&amp;-2 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_3_2_0_n2_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 2&amp; 1/2 \\-1 &amp; 1  \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				Spiral Source, <m>C_1e^{3t/2}\left[\begin{smallmatrix} \cos(t/2) \\ \cos(t/2) - \sin(t/2) \end{smallmatrix}\right] + C_2e^{3t/2}\left[\begin{smallmatrix} \sin(t/2) \\ \sin(t/2) + \cos(t/2) \end{smallmatrix}\right]</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-2-h-n1-1">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 2&amp; 1/2 \\-1 &amp; 1  \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_2_h_n1_1_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
	<task>
		<statement>
			<p>
				<m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 3/2\\ 3/2 &amp; -1 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>
			</p>
		</statement>
		<answer>
			<p>
				 Saddle, <m>C_1\left[\begin{smallmatrix} 3 \\ 1 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{7t/2} + C_2\left[\begin{smallmatrix} -1 \\ 3 \end{smallmatrix}\right]e^{-3t/2}</m>
			</p>
			<figure xml:id="ppsketch-3-3h-3h-n1">
	<caption> Phase portrait sketch for the system <m>\vec{x}'=\begin{pmatrix} 3&amp; 3/2\\ 3/2 &amp; -1 \end{pmatrix}\vec{x}</m>. </caption>
	<image source="Images/phaseportrait_3_3h_3h_n1_sketch.png" width="70%">
		<shortdescription> ALT TEXT HERE </shortdescription>
		<description>
			<p>
				IMAGE DESCRIPTION HERE
			</p>
		</description>
	</image>
	</figure>
		</answer>
	</task>
</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
	<p>
				Consider the second order equation given by 
<md>
y'' + 2y' - 8y = 0.
</md>

			</p>
</introduction>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of this problem using the methods of <xref ref="ho-chapter"/>.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>	
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Convert this equation into a first order linear system using the transformation <m>\vec{x} = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix} y \\ y' \end{smallmatrix} \right]</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>{\vec{x}}' = \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 &amp; 1 \\8 &amp; -2 \end{smallmatrix}\right]\vec{x}</m>
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the eigenvalues and eigenvalues of the coefficient matrix and use that to find the general solution to the system.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Extract the first component of the general solution and compare that to the solution from part (a). How do they relate?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			They are the same!
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Look back through the work. How do the equation used to find the roots in (a) and the eigenvalues in (c) relate to each other?
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>

</exercise>

<exercise>
<introduction>
	<p>
				Consider the second order equation given by 
<md>
y'' + 4y' + 5y = 0.
</md>

			</p>
</introduction>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of this problem using the methods of <xref ref="ho-chapter"/>.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Convert this equation into a first order linear system using the transformation <m>\vec{x} = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix} y \\ y' \end{smallmatrix} \right]</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>{\vec{x}}' = \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 &amp; 1 \\-4 &amp; -4 \end{smallmatrix}\right]\vec{x}</m>
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the eigenvalues and eigenvalues of the coefficient matrix and use that to find the general solution to the system.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Extract the first component of the general solution and compare that to the solution from part (a). How do they relate?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			It's the same, up to potentially needing to rename the constants (<m>D_1 = 2C_1 + C_2</m> and <m>D_2 = 2C_2 - C_1</m>) 
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Look back through the work. How do the equation used to find the roots in (a) and the eigenvalues in (c) relate to each other?
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
			
</exercise>

<exercise>
<introduction>
	<p>
				Consider the second order equation given by 
<md>
y'' - 4y' + 4y = 0.
</md>
 for <m>b</m> and <m>c</m> two real numbers.
			</p>
</introduction>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the general solution of this problem using the methods of <xref ref="ho-chapter"/>.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Convert this equation into a first order linear system using the transformation <m>\vec{x} = \left[ \begin{smallmatrix} y \\ y' \end{smallmatrix} \right]</m>.
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			<m>{\vec{x}}' = \left[\begin{smallmatrix} 0 &amp; 1 \\-4 &amp; 4 \end{smallmatrix}\right]\vec{x}</m>
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Find the eigenvalues and eigenvalues of the coefficient matrix and use that to find the general solution to the system.
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Extract the first component of the general solution and compare that to the solution from part (a). How do they relate?
		</p>
	</statement>
	<answer>
		<p>
			It's the same, up to potentially renaming the constants. 
		</p>
	</answer>
</task>
<task>
	<statement>
		<p>
			Look back through the work. How do the equation used to find the roots in (a) and the eigenvalues in (c) relate to each other?
		</p>
	</statement>
</task>
			
</exercise>
</exercises>

	</section>



